tep_12, step_14). Critically, the 2-hop neighbourhoods of 1357 and 1439 in the co-active period are **completely disjoint** (step_13 vs step_12), so no short cascade is possible.\n\n**The two nodes are temporally anti-correlated.** 1439's activity decays from 34 events early to 0 after t\u224860011; 1357 is silent until t\u224850412 and does most of its work after 60011 (step_06, step_07). The only overlap is the thin band [51612, 60011], with ~5 events each.\n\n**The candidate chain fails ordering.** Refining that band (step_08/09, step_15/16):\n- 1357's earliest event that could coincide with any chain-node (1376/818/786/1539) activity is in bin [55212, 55811]; chain-node activity before that (54012\u201355211) has no matching 1357 event within 600.\n- Incoming events to 1439 occur only in bins [51612,52811], [54012,55211] and [57612,58811] (step_09). But chain nodes 1376/818/786/1539 have **zero** events in [57612,58811] (step_16), so that last arrival came from 1344/1544, not 1539.\n- Hence the only possible 1539\u21921439 hops occur **at or before ~55211**, i.e. before the earliest feasible 1357\u21921376 departure. The chain runs backwards in time.\n\nNo 600-unit-gap-respecting sequence from 1357 to 1439 can be assembled.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_ada3f151\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1357, 1439, 1376, 818, 786, 1539],\n  \"window\": [36012, 74411],\n  \"confidence\": 0.79,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1357 and 1439 are both high-degree and are connected when time is ignored, but only through a 5-hop path (1357-1376-818-786-1539-1439); their 2-hop neighbourhoods in the co-active band are disjoint. Their activity profiles barely overlap: 1439 fades out before 60011 while 1357 only ramps up after 50412. Within the narrow overlap, all arrivals into 1439 that could come from 1539 occur at or before ~55211, whereas the earliest feasible 1357 departure toward the chain is at/after 55212, and the chain nodes are silent in the later bins. The putative path therefore runs backwards in time and no chain of hops with gaps <= 600 connects 1357 to 1439.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 76649, "total_output_tokens": 11817, "total_tokens": 88466, "total_latency_ms": 159822, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}